Add --codec to ModelQuantizer

The flag replaces the codec for the matmul bulk only. Convolutions, ada_ln
projections, embedders and 1-D tensors keep the codecs of the per-version
recipe, which is the same split the app's three quantize actions make.
Sixteen call sites go through a bulkCodec helper that returns the recipe's
codec unless overridden, so the default output is unchanged byte for byte.

Palettizing takes hours on a 22B DiT. i8x takes minutes, and it is the only
encoding the Apple Neural Engine accepts.

Only plain i8x has been tested. The K-quant subtypes are wired through but
unexercised. The iq* formats need an importance matrix, which this flag does
not supply, so they quantize poorly.
